  "methodology": {
    "opencode_usage": "Read-only SQLite queries select only the target session's message and part rows within each scenario window, plus session.version. Assistant message usage is summed once per unique row; step-finish totals are a separate cross-check, never added a second time. Auxiliary title/model calls may not appear in native message usage.",
    "other_usage": "Claude native assistant message IDs are deduplicated before summing usage; Codex uses the final fresh-session usage or a resumed-session cumulative delta.",
    "token_semantics": "OpenCode native input excludes cache fields and its normalized output excludes reasoning: observed total equals input + cache_read + cache_write + output + reasoning. Claude input excludes cache and output includes reasoning. Codex input includes cache and output includes reasoning. Fields are kept separate to prevent double counting.",
    "latency": "Wall time includes startup, model/tool execution and terminal completion. OpenCode call latency is native tool state end minus start; Claude latency is tool-use to tool-result elapsed time. The reverse cross-agent sequence and original blocked replay probe ran concurrently. These observations are not a comparative performance benchmark.",
    "tool_counts": "OpenCode tool-part rows are counted once; Claude tool-use IDs are deduplicated. Non-memory payload bodies are excluded from the metrics helper. No matched baseline exists to attribute extra calls, tokens or latency to memory.",
    "quality": "Counts assess only directly observed eligible cases. Null means not evaluated, not zero. Record counts distinguish lifecycle and scope. One sequence is fixture evidence, not a reliability estimate.",
    "cost": "OpenCode's native reported cost can be zero under subscription-backed access despite nonzero usage; zero is not interpreted as free usage. Positive native estimates remain separate from actual charges, which are unknown.",
    "limitations": "Windows behavior only; no macOS/Linux live-agent qualification. Hook context delivery is not directly observed in the native store. The first resumed TUI replay never received its launch prompt; a separate retry used ordinary terminal input and preserves the blocked attempt. Release qualification remains false pending the full release gates.",
    "raw_evidence": "Native transcripts, database files and authenticated inspection snapshots remain in isolated temporary artifacts. This report contains no raw transcript, absolute path, native identifier or authentication material."
  },
